      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "The speaker addresses God as the Lord of Life and Light and as creator, guardian, protector, and king.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "The speaker asks pardon for misdeeds, asks to be taught the Prophet's path, asks for the heart to be washed from sin, and asks to be led to a home of rest for the blessed.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "A divine book is cited as saying that Mustafa is the true and unerring guide.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "Abu Buker, Omer, Othmn, and Al are named in sequence after the Prophet.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "Al is identified as the spouse of Fatima.",
      "category": "relationship",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Mahommed is quoted as saying, \"I am the city of knowledge--he my gate.\"",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "The passage says that a supplicant at Al's shrine enjoys earthly good in this life and eternal bliss in the next.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "The speaker says he rehearses legends from true records and strings pearls of wisdom in his verse.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "The verse is described as a structure pointing to the skies and as a work that destroying time cannot defeat.",
      "category": "object",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
